From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: Let the host interface glue set the DMA mask

nhi_probe() sets a 64-bit streaming and coherent DMA mask on the host
interface device. That width is a property of the PCI host interfaces.
A host interface on another bus can address fewer bits, and its glue
knows how many, so the NHI core should not impose one.

Set the 64-bit mask in nhi_pci_probe() instead, before nhi_probe(), and
document that the caller configures the DMA masks before probing. PCI
host interfaces get the same mask as before; it is now set before the
NHI is reset and its interrupts are set up rather than after.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c          | 3 ---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h          | 5 +++++
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi_platform.c | 5 +++++
 drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c          | 4 ++++
 4 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
index ecfa875bcda..ce71e79d083 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
@@ -1258,9 +1258,6 @@ int nhi_probe(struct tb_nhi *nhi)
 	if (res)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, res, "cannot enable interrupts, aborting\n");
 
-	res = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
-	if (res)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, res, "failed to set DMA mask\n");
 
 	if (nhi->ops->init) {
 		res = nhi->ops->init(nhi);
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
index e0c044b99dc..dec416d774c 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
@@ -35,6 +35,11 @@ void nhi_interrupt_work(struct work_struct *work);
 bool nhi_handle_interrupts(struct tb_nhi *nhi);
 irqreturn_t nhi_msi(int irq, void *data);
 irqreturn_t ring_msix(int irq, void *data);
+/*
+ * The caller must configure the streaming and coherent DMA masks of the
+ * host interface device before probing, and keep its DMA configuration and
+ * IOMMU attachment valid until nhi_remove() has returned.
+ */
 int nhi_probe(struct tb_nhi *nhi);
 void nhi_remove(struct tb_nhi *nhi);
 void nhi_shutdown(struct tb_nhi *nhi);
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi_platform.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi_platform.c
index a371c5231ff..f3ceb865540 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi_platform.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
@@ -291,6 +292,10 @@ static int nhi_plat_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (np->irq < 0)
 		return np->irq;
 
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to set DMA mask\n");
+
 	if (np->data->power_on) {
 		ret = np->data->power_on(np);
 		if (ret)
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
index c012509feb0..fde7d93bd6e 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
@@ -473,6 +473,10 @@ static int nhi_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *id)
 	nhi_pci_check_quirks(nhi_pci);
 	nhi_pci_check_iommu(nhi_pci);
 
+	res = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+	if (res)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, res, "failed to set DMA mask\n");
+
 	pci_set_master(pdev);
 
 	return nhi_probe(&nhi_pci->nhi);
-- 
